        "lead_summary": "The fortress took the Fed's first hike in three years and did not yield an inch: XLV +1.8% to $168.39, the 50-day reclaimed on Monday and defended all week, while the bombs of two weeks ago reversed \u2014 AMGN +2.2% off the Lp(a) wreck, SYK flat at its low, and the oversold medtech pile (TMO +6.9%, ISRG +6.6%, DHR +5.8%) produced the sector's best snapback of the year. Eli Lilly printed new all-time highs above $1T again. The week's two honest wounds: CVS -6.2% on no headline, and an XBI that +0.3%'d \u2014 alive, but still under its 50-day while IOVA +19% and SDGR +52% proved the event money never left biotech, it just got pickier.",
